<section class="oh-policy-section" id="responsable"><h2>1. Data controller and contact</h2><p>The controller responsible for processing through this website is <strong>Socrates One Web Design LTDA</strong>, trading as <strong>Sócrates Creative Studio / Sócrates ONE</strong>, Brazilian CNPJ <strong>55.962.266/0001-07</strong>. For general contact and privacy requests, email <a href="mailto:info@socrates.la">info@socrates.la</a> with “ONE HUB Privacy” in the subject.</p><p>This is the controller contact channel; it does not imply the formal appointment of a Data Protection Officer where none has been publicly announced. Any appointment duties depend on applicable regulations and the organization’s circumstances.</p></section>
<section class="oh-policy-section" id="informacion"><h2>2. Information we collect</h2><ul><li><strong>Download requests:</strong> name, email address, requested edition (CLEAN, DEMO or COMPLETE), language and registration date/time.</li><li><strong>Download link clicks:</strong> previously registered email, selected edition, language and date/time of a click leading to the GitHub file. A click does not prove completion of the download.</li><li><strong>Contact messages:</strong> the name, email address and message you choose to send.</li><li><strong>Technical data:</strong> hosting systems may handle IP addresses, browser and device details, timestamps, requested URLs, error reports and security logs.</li><li><strong>Preferences and sessions:</strong> selected language, cookie notice preference and technical sessions used by the form and admin dashboard.</li></ul><p>We do not require credit card details, identity documents or sensitive personal information to access downloads. Please do not send passwords or third-party personal information in messages.</p></section>
<section class="oh-policy-section" id="finalidades"><h2>3. Purposes of processing</h2><ul><li>Handle download requests and provide official GitHub links.</li><li>Prevent automated abuse and protect forms, sessions and the private dashboard.</li><li>Count requests and clicks by edition to understand project interest, preferably in aggregated form.</li><li>Respond to support inquiries, rights requests and incidents.</li><li>Maintain website availability and comply with applicable legal duties.</li></ul><p><strong>Download addresses are not enrolled in advertising, newsletters or EMAILSEND marketing campaigns without a separate, appropriate authorization.</strong> There is no payment requirement to use the free software.</p></section>
<section class="oh-policy-section" id="base-legal"><h2>4. Legal bases</h2><p>Depending on the purpose and applicable law, processing may rely on steps requested by you to provide access or respond to your inquiry, appropriately assessed legitimate interests in security and proportionate operational statistics, and compliance with legal obligations. Future promotional communications will require an appropriate legal basis and specific consent where applicable. Acknowledging this policy <strong>is not marketing consent</strong>.</p><p>Relevant Brazilian legislation includes the <a href="https://www.planalto.gov.br/ccivil_03/_ato2015-2018/2018/lei/l13709compilado.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">General Personal Data Protection Law (LGPD, Law 13.709/2018)</a> and the Marco Civil da Internet where applicable.</p></section>
<section class="oh-policy-section" id="procedencia"><h2>5. Source of data and optional registration</h2><p>You provide your name and email directly in the website form. They are necessary to use <em>that particular registration form</em>, but <strong>registration on our site is not required to exercise open-source rights</strong>: the public repository and GitHub Releases are available directly at <a href="https://github.com/socrates-one-web/one-hub" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>. You do not need to donate or purchase professional services.</p></section>
<section class="oh-policy-section" id="almacenamiento"><h2>6. Storage and access</h2><p>Website registration details are stored as CSV files in a private directory on the hosting server and may be viewed through a password-protected administrator dashboard. Access should be limited to authorized personnel. The software includes web access restrictions for that directory, but their effectiveness depends on the server configuration and must be checked at deployment. Registration records are not published in the source repository.</p><p>The hosting provider may handle technical information to provide infrastructure, backups and security. No system can promise absolute protection.</p></section>
<section class="oh-policy-section" id="plazos"><h2>7. Retention and deletion</h2><p>As an operational policy, download requests and click records are reviewed periodically with a <strong>target retention period of up to 12 months</strong>, unless a legal duty, outstanding request or legitimate claim requires a different period. Deletion may require an administrator’s manual action: <strong>the software does not guarantee automatic purging on the expiry date</strong>. Backups may follow a different lifecycle. Technical hosting logs are subject to the provider’s policies and applicable rules, including the Marco Civil when relevant.</p><p>Early deletion requests will be assessed and fulfilled where required, subject to any lawful retention exceptions.</p></section>
<section class="oh-policy-section" id="proveedores"><h2>8. External providers, links and payments</h2><ul><li><strong>GitHub:</strong> hosts source code, the releases and GitHub Sponsors. Using those links is governed by GitHub’s own terms and privacy notice.</li><li><strong>Stripe and Mercado Pago:</strong> provide external voluntary contribution pages and process payments under their own policies. This ONE HUB website does not collect the card numbers you enter there.</li><li><strong>Google Fonts:</strong> the browser may request web fonts from Google servers, disclosing technical connection details.</li><li><strong>Hosting and email services:</strong> operate the website, deliver messages and support infrastructure protection.</li></ul><p>External links do not mean we sell registration lists to these providers, nor do we control their independent privacy practices. Review their notices before submitting data.</p></section>
<section class="oh-policy-section" id="transferencias"><h2>9. International processing</h2><p>GitHub, Google Fonts and payment processors may handle technical connection data and information you provide directly to them in countries outside Brazil. Each provider has its own notices and legal transfer mechanisms. Where this website controller makes a transfer subject to the LGPD, the applicable international-transfer requirements must be observed. We do not claim that all servers or subprocessors are in a single country.</p></section>
<section class="oh-policy-section" id="cookies"><h2>10. Cookies, sessions and local storage</h2><p>The landing uses browser local storage to remember language and cookie notice preferences. Download requests and the private administrator dashboard use technical session cookies needed for security and operation. The reviewed website code does not include advertising pixels or automatic commercial profiling by default. You may clear browser storage, which can reset preferences or terminate a session.</p><p>Third-party websites may use their own cookies once you navigate to them. Read our <a href="cookies.php?lang=en">Cookie Policy</a> for more information.</p></section>
<section class="oh-policy-section" id="seguridad"><h2>11. Security controls and limitations</h2><p>We use proportionate technical and organizational measures such as form validation, controlled sessions, restricted private directories and password-protected administration. The administrator must maintain current PHP versions, credentials, file permissions and backups. Actual security also depends on correct hosting configuration.</p><p>No environment is risk-free. If a security incident occurs, the necessary mitigation and notification measures will be assessed under applicable law.</p></section>
<section class="oh-policy-section" id="derechos"><h2>12. Your personal-data rights</h2><p>Subject to the LGPD and other applicable law, you may request, where legally available, confirmation of processing, access, correction, anonymization, blocking or deletion of excessive or unlawful data, portability, information about sharing, information about the choice to withhold consent and its consequences, review of automated decisions where applicable, and withdrawal of consent previously granted.</p><p>Email <a href="mailto:info@socrates.la?subject=ONE%20HUB%20Privacy">info@socrates.la</a> and identify the address used to register. We may reasonably verify your identity before disclosing or deleting information to prevent misuse. You may contact Brazil’s <a href="https://www.gov.br/anpd/pt-br" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ANPD</a> or another competent authority where applicable.</p></section>
<section class="oh-policy-section" id="menores"><h2>13. Children and young people</h2><p>The site and business management software are not specifically directed at children and are not designed to collect their personal data. A parent or guardian who identifies a registration involving a child without a proper legal basis may request review and deletion.</p></section>
<section class="oh-policy-section" id="instalaciones"><h2>14. Independently hosted installations</h2><p>Organizations downloading and hosting ONE HUB Community on their own servers determine the purposes and means of processing within those deployments and must provide their own privacy notices and safeguards. Publishing open-source code does not grant Sócrates Creative Studio automatic access to their clients, personnel or databases. Specific paid hosting or support arrangements may define additional responsibilities.</p></section>
<section class="oh-policy-section" id="cambios"><h2>15. Policy changes</h2><p>We may update this policy for technical, provider or regulatory changes, displaying the current version and revision date. If a change requires additional notice or specific consent, the applicable procedure will be followed. Merely visiting the website does not constitute consent to new processing requiring authorization.</p></section>
